explanation:
The class states the standard axioms for a topology:
- the whole space is open;
- the intersection of two open sets is open, which gives closure under all finite intersections by induction (the empty intersection is the whole space, already covered);
- the union of any family of open sets is open.

The axiom that the empty set is open is not listed, but it follows from the union axiom applied to the empty family, since ⋃₀ ∅ = ∅. Every type X is allowed, including the empty type, so the definition has the natural generality. This is Mathlib's own basic definition, so there is no other Mathlib counterpart.
